      "title": "AI agent race exposes cloud computing costs and uncertain paths to profit",
      "content_html": "AI agents designed to keep working in the cloud face a cost challenge: extended tasks can require repeated model calls, and heavier use may raise operating expenses even as individual calls become cheaper, developers and analysts told Huxiu. Anthropic’s Claude Duet, a work-focused agent released in research preview on Oct. 21, is competing with Meta’s Muse and OpenAI’s Dots.\n\nInterviewees said profitability depends on computing costs, sustained use and a viable revenue model. Workplace agents may be easier to sell because businesses can weigh completed reports or customer follow-ups against labor saved, but data protection, permissions and software integrations add costs.",
